K41c  found  mini-registry/docs/GAPS-PAPER.md:179
    claim: Capital letters set aside are exercised by the data only where one of the 8 differs in capitals only
    words: so that line 13's «(capitals ignored)» is exercised by the data
    line : **A conflict, and how this paper resolves it.** The first edition proposed that some of the 8 differ in capitals only, so that line 13's «(capitals ignored)» is exercised by the data. Register line 172 compares family names «letter for letter»: if that comparison heeds capitals, a child whose family name differs in capitals only is counted as spelt differently, and R-12 counts more than 4. This paper drops the capitals-only children: under setting 2 below, R-12 counts 4 whether its comparison heeds capitals or not, and «(capitals ignored)» is still exercised, by R-05's test (b) at register line 79. The other way out — keeping capitals-only children and having round 2 read register line 172 as capitals ignored — would read into an accepted test and is not recommended.
